Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-28-2001||11:39 AM||||Is there a big difference between the seats in a 88 Formula and a 88 GT. Comfort level, side support, appearance?||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-28-2001||12:10 PM||||all I think are same seat, just diff covers. at least all ive had were.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||01-28-2001||12:39 PM||||I have had both and they are exactly the same, just different covers as RogerGarrison stated.<P>The GT's are alittle more "prettier" than the Formula/Coupe's.<P>AND they are the same through out the Fiero line (Except for the speakers in the top of the seats in 84-85 and the lumbar option in the 88).<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-28-2001||01:47 PM||||The seats are the same (except for the lumbar option), but the material is different.  The '88 GT material is more durable than the coupe/Formula.  That is why you rarely see '88 GT cloth seats with rips.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rodmcneill||01-28-2001||08:56 PM||||Thanks for the reply's. The reason I asked this question was that I have the video tape that the Fiero Store sells and in it when Motor Week compares the 88 Formula to the Toyota MR2 they complain that the Formula needs more side bolstering in the seat and that quote "the Fiero GT seats have much better support".||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||01-29-2001||11:20 AM||||I get a kick out of that too. All Fieros have the same amount of seat padding & bolster support.||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||01-29-2001||11:31 AM||||all things are relative - maybe the Formula <I>they</I> drove needed more padding.........as for the seats - they are all the same.........but, I can get in someone elses car and it <I>feels</I> different from my own so, the amount of padding felt is in direct proportion to the amount of padding the owner had when driving the car..........||||reg||1
